    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d916">

                <pb facs="0901" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg789"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24/512: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-23T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 23,
                                1919—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9404. Am[erican] mission’s 5558, December 5, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>Department of State regrets sale of supplies to Ukrainians by Liquidation
                    Committee and would welcome any action to annul its effects which would not
                    embarrass American authorities. Department concurs as to undesirability of
                    Ukrainians obtaining funds in France through sale of supplies. See Department’s
                    3749 November 13, 2 p.m. to Am[erican] mission.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d916-f1"/>
                    Distribution of that portion consisting of medical supplies by Red Cross now
                    under consideration and will be discussed with Polk. Can you devise method to prevent Ukrainian use of other
                    supplies?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
